=begin pod :id<showcase> :toc

=TITLE Podlite highlighting showcase

=begin SYNOPSIS
A section name like SYNOPSIS or SEE-ALSO reads in its own colour, apart from a
standard block and apart from a name you brought in yourself.
=end SYNOPSIS

=head1 Block names come in four kinds

=begin nested
A standard block: C<=head>, C<=item>, C<=code>, C<=table>, C<=nested>.
=end nested

=begin picture :caption('a name the author brought in')
podlite-mark-desktop.svg
=end picture

=for Diagram :caption('another one')
graph TD; A-->B;

=head1 Markup codes

Basic text: B<bold>, I<italic>, U<underlined>, C<inline code>, O<struck out>.

Links: L<the project site|https://podlite.org> and a contextual backlink
W<markup codes|defn:markup-code>. The part after the bar reads apart from the text.

Entities and verbatim: E<copy> E<lt>angle brackets E<gt>, V<no B<markup> here>,
S<spaces   are   kept>.

Marks for the reader: X<index entry>, N<a footnote>, H<above the line>,
J<below the line>, Z<this one never reaches the page>.

Typed text: K<what you type>, T<what the screen shows>, R<a stand-in value>.

Hidden until published: G<this strip stays covered, the caret opens it>.

=alias PRODUCT Podlite Desktop
An alias resolves at render time: A<PRODUCT>.

=head1 Settings and their delimiters

=for para :id<delims> :lang<en> :caption('quoted value') :tags<a b> :!toc
A value in angle brackets, in quotes, a list, and a negated setting — each
delimiter reads as a value, and a hyphenated name stays whole.

=set :caption('a caption for the block that follows')
=begin code :lang<js>
// code inside a block is coloured by the language its settings name
const podlite = require('podlite')
const tree = podlite().parse('=head1 Hello')
console.log(tree.type)
=end code

=head1 Markdown inside Podlite

=begin markdown
The body of this block is read as **Markdown**, and a fence inside it keeps its
own highlighting:

```python
def greet(name: str) -> str:
    return f"hello, {name}"
```
=end markdown

=head1 Tables and data

=begin table :caption('what each delimiter carries')
 Written        | Read as        | Note
 ===============|================|=====================
 :key<a b>      | list           | whitespace separates
 :key<a,b>      | string         | a comma stays
 :key('a b')    | string         | quotes keep it whole
 :key{:a, :b}   | map            | option form
=end table

=begin data :key<sales> :mime-type('text/csv')
month,units
january,120
february,143
=end data

